Errors — Root Causes and Fixes Applied
  
  4 bugs found and fixed:

  #: 1
  Bug: GET /fence → 500, GET /mission → item_timeout
  Root Cause: wait_for_message filtered MISSION_ITEM_INT by mission_type — older ArduPilot sends
    type=0 even for FENCE items. Items 0-1 got through by chance, 2+ were silently dropped, retries

    exhausted
  Fix: Stop filtering MISSION_ITEM_INT/MISSION_ITEM by type at all; for other messages accept
  type=0
    as "unset"
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  #: 2
  Bug: item_timeout after 2 items
  Root Cause: Stale duplicate packets (AP retransmissions) consumed retry attempts — 5 attempts
    spent draining old item-0/1 messages, none left for item-2
  Fix: Inner drain loop: keep reading within the 2.5s window when seq doesn't match, no retry
    consumed
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  #: 3
  Bug: Any successful fence download → 500
  Root Cause: MissionItem had no to_dict() method — return {"items": [item.to_dict() for item in 
    items]} would throw AttributeError
  Fix: Added to_dict() to MissionItem
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  #: 4
  Bug: POST /fence/upload → ArduPilot rejects
  Root Cause: Fence items sent with frame=3 (relative altitude). MP source confirms: all fence
  items
    must be frame=0 (MAV_FRAME_GLOBAL)
  Fix: Changed buildMissionItemsForType to use frame: 0 for FENCE

  Files changed: mission_manager.py, mission_models.py, FlightPlanner.jsx

