  Plan Tab — How MP Implements It vs. Ours
  
  Type selector (MISSION / FENCE / RALLY): MP stores three separate in-memory buffers (MAV.wps,
  MAV.fencepoints, MAV.rallypoints). Switching type saves the current buffer and restores the
  target buffer. We now match this exactly with _missionSaved/_fenceSaved/_rallySaved (just
  implemented this session).

  FENCE protocol: MP's modern path uses MAV_MISSION_TYPE_FENCE (what we use). Forces
  frame=MAV_FRAME_GLOBAL (0) on all fence items before upload (we now do this too). param1 on each
  vertex item = total vertex count of that polygon. No minimum vertex count enforcement — same as
  ours.

  Click-to-add: MP in fence mode hides the "Add" button and expects polygon drawing tool. We use
  map click-to-add vertices, which works but is less constrained.

  What MP has that we don't yet: Circle fence types (FENCE_CIRCLE_INCLUSION,
  FENCE_CIRCLE_EXCLUSION), survey grid lawnmower generation, per-command parameter help text in the
   waypoint table, spline waypoints.